## Authentication
API Key (x-goog-api-key) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (2)
- `GET /v1/projects/{projectToken}/settings` — Get settings for a specific project.
- `POST /$rpc/{$rpcToken}/GenerateIT` — Generate an IT using an RPC token.

### Data Read (3)
- `GET /api/v1/ip` — Determine the IP address of the request.
- `GET /attribution_trigger` — Trigger attribution tracking.
- `GET /resources/cards/{cardId}/` — Retrieve details for a specific card.

### Data Write (2)
- `POST /v1/p` — Create or update a post.
- `POST /wa/` — Send a message via WhatsApp.

### Media (1)
- `GET /_next/image` — Retrieve an image from the Buffer CDN.

### Core API (1)
- `GET /next-api/helpscout` — Get Help Scout data for troubleshooting.

## Quick Start

### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow
- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).
- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.
- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode="backend"`.

Example:
```text
unbrowse_replay { service: "buffer", executionMode: "backend", endpoint: "GET /api/v1/ip" }
```

Here are a few examples to get you started using the Buffer API:

```typescript
// Retrieve settings for a specific project.  Requires authentication.
async function getProjectSettings(projectToken: string) {
  try {
    const settings = await client.get_v1_projects_projectToken_settings({ projectToken });
    console.log("Project Settings:", settings);
    return settings;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Failed to retrieve project settings:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

```typescript
